KG42.register("rules-4bf1d5d380fa7c60b6156f14",{"id":"33-retail_market_interoperability::v141-c-R009","paper":"33-retail_market_interoperability","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R009","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Local clearing price","process_stage":"pricing","market_meaning":"Submitted demand bids are inputs to the local MCP calculation alongside the optimal participant schedules. Scope: Proposed local retail market for H-MGs and retailers; day-ahead double-sided forward auction. Submitted supply bids are inputs to the local MCP calculation alongside the optimal participant schedules. Scope: Proposed local retail market for H-MGs and retailers; day-ahead double-sided forward auction. The optimal participant allocations obtained through Nash-equilibrium scheduling are inputs to the local MCP calculation. Scope: Proposed local retail market; Nash-equilibrium participant allocations supplied to the double-sided forward auction. The market operator calculates the optimum local market price using information received from buyers and sellers. Scope: Proposed retail electricity market shared by H-MGs and retailers. The MCP is set at the intersection of the aggregated supply and demand curves. Scope: Local market pricing through the forward double-sided auction.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function pricing.local under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["bidding.demand","bidding.supply","clearing.local","coordination.local_operator","pricing.local"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R009-E001","source":"bidding.demand","target":"pricing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R009-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g02-e032"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R009-E002","source":"bidding.supply","target":"pricing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R009-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g02-e032"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R009-E003","source":"clearing.local","target":"pricing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R009-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e032"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R009-E004","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"pricing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R009-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Local market pricing through the forward double-sided auction. | Proposed local retail market for H-MGs and retailers; day-ahead double-sided forward auction. | Proposed local retail market; Nash-equilibrium participant allocations supplied to the double-sided forward auction. | Proposed retail electricity market shared by H-MGs and retailers.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g02-e032"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R009-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Submitted demand bids are inputs to the local MCP calculation alongside the optimal participant schedules. Scope: Proposed local retail market for H-MGs and retailers; day-ahead double-sided forward auction.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g02-e032"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R009-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Submitted supply bids are inputs to the local MCP calculation alongside the optimal participant schedules. Scope: Proposed local retail market for H-MGs and retailers; day-ahead double-sided forward auction.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E16","v141-b-g02-e032"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R009-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The optimal participant allocations obtained through Nash-equilibrium scheduling are inputs to the local MCP calculation. Scope: Proposed local retail market; Nash-equilibrium participant allocations supplied to the double-sided forward auction.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e032"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R009-C004","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The market operator calculates the optimum local market price using information received from buyers and sellers. Scope: Proposed retail electricity market shared by H-MGs and retailers.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E05"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R009-C005","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The MCP is set at the intersection of the aggregated supply and demand curves. Scope: Local market pricing through the forward double-sided auction.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e032"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E05","location":{"location_id":"src-f979d1e84e-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"3. The proposed retail market structure","anchor_text":"a single H-MG can have both generator and consumer as players in the market. This feature is preferr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The market operator (MO) is the entity who manages the retail market and its participants. The MO could be either a separate entity overseen by the distribution network operator (DNO) or the distribution management system (DMS) or a part of existing distribution system operator (DSO)/DMS which alternatively becomes a flexible DSO. In any case, the functionalities of the proposed market structure will remain the same. The optimum price is calculated by the MO using information received from buyers and sellers."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E16","location":{"location_id":"src-f979d1e84e-p05-c2r4__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"3. The proposed retail market structure","anchor_text":"upfront cost of required devices to participate in the market for each H-MG, which encourages more p","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"From Step 2, the shortage and excess power of each H-MG is known for every scenario without considering the retailers and interoperability among H-MGs. In Step 3, however, a scheduling problem is solved (in the PBUC unit) in the presence of participating retailers and power shortage/surplus of each H-MG. As it is shown in Fig. 3, each retailer participates in the market by submitting two separate sets of bids: bid-in demand for purchasing excess power from H-MGs, and bid-in supply for selling power to support H-MGs with power shortage. Bids are submitted in the form of blocks of price and energy quantity. Step 3 also determines the upper limit for sold/purchased power to/from each retailer while maximizing exploitation of the H-MG generation. Further details are given in Section 4."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e032","location":{"location_id":"src-f979d1e84e-p07-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"6. MCP unit","anchor_text":"by the participants using a forward market with a double-sided auc- ess tion [52]. The forward marke","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In this unit, MCP is calculated based on the schedules obtained from the Nash equilibrium calculation (i.e. optimum capacity of each player in the market) and supply and demand bids submitted by the participants using a forward market with a double-sided auction [52]. The forward market aggregates the supply and demand in the merit order in terms of price-quantity pairs. The quantities are optimal schedules obtained from Step 4, and the prices are supply and demand bids submitted by the players. As expected, the aggregated supply and demand quantity-price values are monotonically increasing and decreasing step-wise curves, respectively. MCP will be the intersection of the aggregated supply and demand curves. Finally, the pay-off function will be computed for each player based on the MCP."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"No explicit decision-variable symbol for the local MCP is defined in the supplied MCP-unit evidence. The source names the acronym MCP and describes curve intersection, while Eq. (5) defines an H-MG load offer price, not an MCP variable. No x is therefore declared.","empty_theta_reason":"The supplied MCP-unit text gives no explicit coefficients or numerical parameters for forming the intersection of aggregated supply and demand. Parameters such as theta and beta in Eq. (5) belong to the H-MG load offer-price formula and are not imported into this rule without a supported MCP relation."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-participation","v141-a-M01-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e032","quote":"In this unit, MCP is calculated based on the schedules obtained from the Nash equilibrium calculation (i.e. optimum capacity of each player in the market) and supply and demand bids submitted by the participants using a forward market with a double-sided auction [52]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E16","quote":"Bids are submitted in the form of blocks of price and energy quantity."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e032","quote":"In this unit, MCP is calculated based on the schedules obtained from the Nash equilibrium calculation (i.e. optimum capacity of each player in the market) and supply and demand bids submitted by the participants using a forward market with a double-sided auction [52]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E16","quote":"Bids are submitted in the form of blocks of price and energy quantity."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e032","quote":"MCP is calculated based on the schedules obtained from the Nash equilibrium calculation (i.e. optimum capacity of each player in the market)"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E05","quote":"The optimum price is calculated by the MO using information received from buyers and sellers."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e032","quote":"MCP will be the intersection of the aggregated supply and demand curves."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"b9886e29d777e5a72789153b2eaaca932c9108adaed194c0818978dc3cebb11c","applicability":"needs_revision","reason":"The supplied source evidence describes the local MCP verbally as the intersection of aggregated supply and demand curves, but it provides no explicit algebraic MCP equation and no symbol definition for the MCP price itself. Eq. (5), present elsewhere in the evidence catalog, defines an H-MG load offer price rather than the MCP intersection. The frozen rule graph also contains no nodes or edges for aggregated supply/demand curves. Therefore the five C.1 constraints remain procedural and not formalized; no supported mathematical expression can be added without changing the frozen graph or inventing missing symbols.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R009-C001","node_ids":["bidding.demand","pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R009-E001"],"rationale":"Source evidence states that supply and demand bids submitted by participants are inputs to the MCP calculation in the double-sided forward auction. The frozen edge E001 links bidding.demand to pricing.local for this relation; the C.1 constraint is retained as a procedural input relation, not a formal algebraic MCP equation."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R009-C002","node_ids":["bidding.supply","pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R009-E002"],"rationale":"Source evidence states that supply bids are among the inputs to the local MCP calculation. The frozen edge E002 links bidding.supply to pricing.local; the constraint is retained as a procedural input relation."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R009-C003","node_ids":["clearing.local","pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R009-E003"],"rationale":"Source evidence states that MCP is calculated from schedules obtained through the Nash-equilibrium calculation, i.e. optimal participant capacities from the equilibrium step. The frozen edge E003 links clearing.local to pricing.local; no further algebraic MCP formula is supplied."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R009-C004","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator","pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R009-E004"],"rationale":"Source evidence states that the market operator calculates the optimum price using information received from buyers and sellers. The frozen edge E004 links coordination.local_operator to pricing.local; the source does not provide an operator-level pricing formula."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R009-C005","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Source evidence states that MCP will be the intersection of the aggregated supply and demand curves. The frozen graph has no dedicated aggregate supply-curve or aggregate demand-curve nodes or edges, so this remains a property attached to pricing.local only and is not formalized."}],"revision_requests":["C.1: confirm whether the source contains an explicit MCP symbol or equation for the intersection of aggregated supply and demand curves. If yes, extract the symbol definition, domain, and any supporting graph nodes/edges; if no, keep the rule as procedural/non-algebraic rather than inventing an MCP formula.","C.1: clarify whether aggregated supply and aggregated demand curves are intended as representable graph objects. The frozen rule graph currently has no curve nodes or edges, so C.2 cannot bind a formal intersection condition to them.","C.1: distinguish the H-MG load offer price in Eq. (5) from the local MCP. Eq. (5) is supported elsewhere in the evidence catalog, but it is not the MCP intersection and must not be substituted for it without source support."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
